    {
      "id": "01",
      "title": "Uploading huge files",
      "question": "How do users upload multi-gigabyte videos reliably?",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "type": "question",
          "say": "YouTube, question one. Users upload videos that are several gigabytes. How do you make uploads fast, and resilient to flaky networks? Pause and answer out loud.",
          "pauseAfter": 3,
          "props": {
            "question": "Multi-gigabyte uploads: <em>fast</em> and <em>resilient</em>?"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "graph",
          "say": "First the client asks the upload service for permission. It authenticates the user, and returns a presigned URL: temporary, write-only access to one object in storage. The client splits the video into chunks of five to ten megabytes, and uploads them straight to object storage, so the bulk traffic bypasses the application servers. If a chunk fails, the client retries just that chunk, not the whole file. When every chunk has landed, storage fires an event onto the transcoding queue.",
          "props": {
            "title": "Straight to storage, <em>chunk by chunk</em>",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "id": "client",
                "label": "Client",
                "x": 170,
                "y": 520,
                "w": 180,
                "h": 70
              },
              {
                "id": "up",
                "label": "Upload service",
                "x": 660,
                "y": 270,
                "w": 260,
                "h": 70
              },
              {
                "id": "store",
                "label": "Object storage\n(raw)",
                "x": 980,
                "y": 480,
                "w": 260,
                "h": 90
              },
              {
                "id": "queue",
                "label": "Transcode queue",
                "x": 980,
                "y": 680,
                "w": 260,
                "h": 60,
                "hidden": true
              }
            ],
            "edges": [
              {
                "from": "client",
                "to": "up",
                "w": "POST /uploads"
              },
              {
                "from": "client",
                "to": "store",
                "w": "PUT chunk k"
              }
            ],
            "panels": [
              {
                "key": "chunks",
                "label": "Chunks",
                "type": "list",
                "rows": 1,
                "initial": []
              }
            ],
            "steps": [
              {
                "at": "asks",
                "nodes": {
                  "client": "active"
                },
                "edges": {
                  "client-up": "relax"
                },
                "note": "Ask to upload"
              },
              {
                "at": "temporary",
                "add": [
                  {
                    "from": "up",
                    "to": "client",
                    "w": "presigned URL"
                  }
                ],
                "nodes": {
                  "client": "base",
                  "up": "active"
                },
                "edges": {
                  "client-up": "base",
                  "up-client": "relax"
                },
                "note": "Auth, then a presigned URL: temporary, write-only"
              },
              {
                "at": "splits",
                "nodes": {
                  "up": "base",
                  "client": "active"
                },
                "edges": {
                  "up-client": "base",
                  "client-store": "relax"
                },
                "panels": {
                  "chunks": [
                    "1 ✓",
                    "2 ✓"
                  ]
                },
                "note": "5–10 MB chunks, straight to storage"
              },
              {
                "at": "bypasses",
                "nodes": {
                  "up": "dim"
                },
                "note": "Bulk traffic bypasses the app servers"
              },
              {
                "at": "fails",
                "edges": {
                  "client-store": "dim"
                },
                "panels": {
                  "chunks": [
                    "1 ✓",
                    "2 ✓",
                    "3 ✗"
                  ]
                },
                "note": "Chunk 3 fails…"
              },
              {
                "at": "retries",
                "edges": {
                  "client-store": "relax"
                },
                "panels": {
                  "chunks": [
                    "1 ✓",
                    "2 ✓",
                    "3 ✓",
                    "4 ✓"
                  ]
                },
                "note": "…retry only chunk 3"
              },
              {
                "at": "landed",
                "show": [
                  "queue"
                ],
                "add": [
                  {
                    "from": "store",
                    "to": "queue",
                    "w": "all chunks in"
                  }
                ],
                "nodes": {
                  "client": "base",
                  "up": "base",
                  "store": "done"
                },
                "edges": {
                  "client-store": "base",
                  "store-queue": "relax"
                },
                "note": "Complete → event to the transcode queue"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "02",
      "title": "The transcoding DAG",
      "question": "What happens between upload and ready to play?",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "type": "question",
          "say": "Question two. A raw video has landed in storage. What has to happen before anyone can play it? Pause and answer out loud.",
          "pauseAfter": 3,
          "props": {
            "question": "Between <em>uploaded</em> and <em>ready to play</em>?"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "graph",
          "say": "The upload event lands on a queue, and a workflow orchestrator picks it up, and runs the processing as a DAG. First it inspects the raw file: codec, resolution and frame rate decide the outputs. Then transcoding jobs run in parallel, one per resolution and format, on a CPU-heavy worker fleet, with thumbnails extracted alongside. Each output is cut into segments a few seconds long, plus a manifest that lists every quality. Segments and manifests go to processed storage. Only when the whole DAG finishes is the video marked ready, in the metadata database.",
          "props": {
            "title": "Processing as a <em>DAG</em>",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "id": "queue",
                "label": "Queue",
                "x": 170,
                "y": 470,
                "w": 150,
                "h": 60
              },
              {
                "id": "orch",
                "label": "Orchestrator",
                "x": 430,
                "y": 470,
                "w": 220,
                "h": 64
              },
              {
                "id": "insp",
                "label": "Inspect",
                "x": 700,
                "y": 470,
                "w": 170,
                "h": 64
              },
